# --- Canonical host: force www -> apex (non-www, https) ---
# Belt-and-suspenders. www is registered as a Netlify domain alias, and Netlify
# already 301s the alias -> primary (apex) at the edge. This explicit rule makes
# the www->apex intent visible in version control and survives an accidental
# alias removal. Apex requests (Host: signalroompodcast.com) don't match this
# host-scoped rule, so there is no loop. http://www is upgraded to https://www at
# the TLS edge first, then caught here. Verified live 2026-06-11: www/ -> apex/
# is a single 301; every variant terminates at a clean 200 apex extensionless URL.
https://www.signalroompodcast.com/*    https://signalroompodcast.com/:splat    301!

